{ "cells": [ { "cell\_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": [ "# ⛅ University of Wolverhampton — AI Weather Predictor\\n", "### Welcome Sandwell College Students!\\n", "\\n", "Today, we are going to teach a machine learning model how to predict the weather based on historical data.\\n", "\\n", "\*\*Step 1:\*\* Run the cell below by clicking the \*\*▶ Play button\*\* (or press \`Shift + Enter\`)." ] }, { "cell\_type": "code", "execution\_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": [ "import numpy as np\\n", "import pandas as pd\\n", "\\n", "# 1\. Create 100 days of past weather data with a realistic pattern\\n", "np.random.seed(42)\\n", "days = 100\\n", "yesterday\_temp = np.random.uniform(8, 25, days)\\n", "humidity = np.random.uniform(45, 90, days)\\n", "# Natural relationship: warmer yesterday -&gt; warmer today; higher humidity -&gt; slightly cooler\\n", "today\_temp = (0.8 \* yesterday\_temp) - (0.05 \* humidity) + 3 + np.random.normal(0, 1.2, days)\\n", "\\n", "weather\_df = pd.DataFrame({\\n", " 'Yesterday\_Temp\_C': np.round(yesterday\_temp, 1),\\n", " 'Humidity\_Pct': np.round(humidity, 1),\\n", " 'Today\_Temp\_C': np.round(today\_temp, 1)\\n", "})\\n", "\\n", "print(\\"✅ Data loaded successfully! Here are the first 5 days of history:\\")\\n", "weather\_df.head()" ] }, { "cell\_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": [ "---\\n", "### 🧠 Step 2: Train the AI Model\\n", "\\n", "Now we give our data to \`LinearRegression\`, an AI algorithm that learns the mathematical relationship between the inputs (\`X\`) and the answer (\`y\`).\\n", "\\n", "👉 \*\*YOUR TASK:\*\* In the code below, replace the \`???\` with \`X, y\` so the model can learn from both features and answers!" ] }, { "cell\_type": "code", "execution\_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": [ "from sklearn.linear\_model import LinearRegression\\n", "\\n", "# X is our input clues (features); y is the actual temperature (target)\\n", "X = weather\_df[['Yesterday\_Temp\_C', 'Humidity\_Pct']]\\n", "y = weather\_df['Today\_Temp\_C']\\n", "\\n", "model = LinearRegression()\\n", "\\n", "# TODO: Replace ??? with X, y\\n", "# model.fit(X, y)\\n", "model.fit(???, ???)\\n", "\\n", "print(\\"🎉 Congratulations! Your AI model has learned the weather patterns!\\")" ] }, { "cell\_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": [ "---\\n", "### 🔮 Step 3: Test Your AI on New Weather\\n", "\\n", "Now let's ask the AI to predict today's temperature based on yesterday's temperature and today's humidity.\\n", "\\n", "👉 \*\*YOUR TASK:\*\* Change the values of \`my\_yesterday\_temp\` and \`my\_humidity\`, then run the cell to see the AI's prediction!" ] }, { "cell\_type": "code", "execution\_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": [ "# Try changing these numbers:\\n", "my\_yesterday\_temp = 20.0 # Try a number between 5 and 30\\n", "my\_humidity = 60.0 # Try a percentage between 30 and 100\\n", "\\n", "# Ask the AI model to predict\\n", "prediction = model.predict([[my\_yesterday\_temp, my\_humidity]])[0]\\n", "\\n", "print(f\\"🔮 AI Prediction for Today: {prediction:.1f} °C\\")\\n", "\\n", "if prediction &gt;= 18:\\n", " print(\\"☀️ Outlook: Warm &amp; pleasant! Great day for campus life.\\")\\n", "elif prediction &gt;= 12:\\n", " print(\\"⛅ Outlook: Mild and overcast.\\")\\n", "else:\\n", " print(\\"🌧️ Outlook: Chilly! Grab a coat.\\")" ] } ], "metadata": { "language\_info": { "name": "python" } }, "nbformat": 4, "nbformat\_minor": 2 }
